MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the tier system with defaults that preserve current visuals (auto
-> high). React (Hole2Page) is the single source of truth: holds the
quality preference + resolved tier, renders data-perf on .hole2-stage,
and owns resolveTier/detectTier (reduced-motion -> low for now; Phase 3
adds the device heuristic).

- engine: Hole2Quality/Hole2Tier types, setPerf on the handle (relays to
  onPerfChange; no gameplay knobs), getState reports live quality+tier.
- onPerfChange opt threads through Hole2Game; forcedTier reserved for the
  Phase-3 auto-downgrade (drops visuals without overwriting the pref).
- CSS data-perf gates: MED drops the outer ground-blur pass + tightens
  the inner halo to 14px; LOW keeps the halo (10px, sacred) + the 3
  ghosts (flat) but strips the vignette and the box/boss/player glows.

No UI to change tiers yet (that's Phase 2b); default high = no visual
change. Gameplay is tier-independent.
